Chapter: ShellTypes

  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 A domain-specific type system for shell script generation.
 ShellExpr represents values and conditions. ShellCmd represents
 statements. ShellScript is a complete script with parameters.

 The types are data -- they describe what a script does, not how.
 Emitter functions (PowerShellEmit, BashEmit) pattern-match these
 types and produce target-shell source text.

 We say:

Section: Expressions

  ShellExpr =
    | SeLit (Text)
    | SeInt (Integer)
    | SeVar (Text)
    | SeEnvVar (Text)
    | SeConcat (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeFileExists (ShellExpr)
    | SeDirExists (ShellExpr)
    | SeStringEq (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeStringNeq (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeIntEq (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeIntLt (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeIntGt (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeIntLe (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeIntGe (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeExitCodeEq (Integer)
    | SeNot (ShellExpr)
    | SeAnd (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeOr (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeFileSize (ShellExpr)
    | SeSubstring (ShellExpr) (Integer) (Integer)
    | SeTextLength (ShellExpr)
    | SeIndex (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeProperty (ShellExpr) (Text)
    | SeMethodCall (ShellExpr) (Text) (List ShellExpr)
    | SeStaticCall (Text) (Text) (List ShellExpr)
    | SeMatch (ShellExpr) (Text)
    | SeStartsWith (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeHashLiteral
    | SeArrayLiteral (List ShellExpr)
    | SeBool (Boolean)
    | SeScriptRoot
    | SePathJoin (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SePathParent (ShellExpr)
    | SeNow
    | SeFormatTime (ShellExpr) (Text)
    | SeElapsedSeconds (ShellExpr)
    | SeLastExit
    | SeTailJoin (ShellExpr) (Integer) (ShellExpr)
    | SeErrorText
    | SeCall (Text) (List ShellExpr)
    | SeMatchExpr (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeCount (ShellExpr)
    | SeAdd (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeSubstringFrom (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeListFiles (ShellExpr) (Text) (Boolean)
    | SePathResolve (ShellExpr)
    | SeFileNonEmptyLineCount (ShellExpr)
    | SeItem
    | SePipe (ShellExpr) (List ShellStage)
    | SeJoin (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeTrim (ShellExpr)
    | SeStaticProp (Text) (Text)
    | SeFileFirstLine (ShellExpr)
    | SeNewline
    | SeTab
    | SeCrLf
    | SeContains (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeListGlob (ShellExpr)
    | SeOrderedMap (List ShellField)
    | SeAsArray (ShellExpr)
    | SeCallArgs (Text) (List ShellArg)
    | SeReplace (ShellExpr) (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | SeToLower (ShellExpr)
    | SeLines (List ShellExpr)
    | SeSlice (ShellExpr) (Integer) (Integer)
    | SeSplit (ShellExpr) (Text)
    | SeMul (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeSub (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeDiv (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeCast (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | SeFormat (ShellExpr) (List ShellExpr)
    | SeRecord (List ShellField)
    | SeHasField (ShellExpr) (Text)
    | SeIfElse (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeSubstringLen (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | SeFileText (ShellExpr)
    | SeRaw (Text)

Section: Arguments

 A command's arguments are named, switched or positional. Spelling them as
 bare text would put the target shell's flag syntax into the caller, which
 is what this whole type exists to keep out.

  ShellArg =
    | SaPos (ShellExpr)
    | SaNamed (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | SaSwitch (Text)

Section: Records

 A field of a record literal. The commonest shape a build script still could
 not say is a TABLE of cases walked by a loop, where some cases carry an
 extra field the others do not.

  ShellField =
    | SfField (Text) (ShellExpr)

Section: Colour

 The sixteen named terminal colours, and they are named rather than carried
 as an Rgb on purpose. Foreword chapter Color and Punctual chapter ColorOps
 are both PIXEL colour, packed channels for framebuffers and real-time
 compositing; a console takes neither. What every target we might emit to
 does share is this sixteen: a ConsoleColor value, an ANSI SGR code in
 30-37 and 90-97, and a Windows console attribute nibble. So the sixteen
 are the portable intersection and an arbitrary triple is not.

 A target that cannot colour drops the attribute and keeps the text.

  ShellColor =
    | ClBlack
    | ClRed
    | ClGreen
    | ClYellow
    | ClBlue
    | ClMagenta
    | ClCyan
    | ClWhite
    | ClBrightBlack
    | ClBrightRed
    | ClBrightGreen
    | ClBrightYellow
    | ClBrightBlue
    | ClBrightMagenta
    | ClBrightCyan
    | ClBrightWhite

Section: Sequences

 A pipeline is a source, a chain of transforms, and a terminal. Counted
 across the tree the transforms are filter, map, take and sort and nothing
 else, so the type says those four rather than admitting arbitrary stages;
 an escape hatch here would rot the way the raw command did.

 SeItem is the element under the cursor. Naming it rather than binding a
 variable keeps the stage expressions target-independent, since the spelling
 of the cursor is the emitter's business.

  ShellStage =
    | StWhere (ShellExpr)
    | StMap (ShellExpr)
    | StTake (Integer)
    | StSort
    | StSortBy (Text)
    | StSortDesc (Text)

Section: Commands

  ShellCmd =
    | ScRun (Text) (List ShellExpr)
    | ScRunDot (ShellExpr)
    | ScAssign (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScEcho (ShellExpr)
    | ScWriteError (ShellExpr)
    | ScCopy (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | ScMove (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | ScDelete (ShellExpr)
    | ScMkdir (ShellExpr)
    | ScWriteFile (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | ScReadFile (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScReadBytes (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScWriteBytes (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | ScIf (ShellExpr) (List ShellCmd) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScFor (Text) (ShellExpr) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScWhile (ShellExpr) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScBreak
    | ScContinue
    | ScReturn (ShellExpr)
    | ScExit (ShellExpr)
    | ScTry (List ShellCmd) (List ShellCmd) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScSequence (List ShellCmd)
    | ScComment (Text)
    | ScBlank
    | ScStartProcess (ShellProcessSpec)
    | ScWaitProcess (Text) (Integer)
    | ScHashFile (Text) (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScTempFile (Text)
    | ScSetStrictMode
    | ScSetErrorStop
    | ScForEach (Text) (ShellExpr) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScForLoop (Text) (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScLabeledWhile (Text) (ShellExpr) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScContinueLabel (Text)
    | ScDotNetCall (Text) (Text) (List ShellExpr)
    | ScDotNetCallAssign (Text) (Text) (Text) (List ShellExpr)
    | ScSetContent (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | ScAddContent (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | ScSetErrorContinue
    | ScSetLocation (ShellExpr)
    | ScIncrement (Text)
    | ScDecrement (Text)
    | ScAppend (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScRunCapture (ShellExpr) (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScFunction (Text) (List ShellParam) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScDiscard (ShellExpr)
    | ScIncrementBy (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScRunArgs (ShellExpr) (List ShellArg)
    | ScRunArgsDropErr (ShellExpr) (List ShellArg)
    | ScPrintFile (ShellExpr)
    | ScPipeDo (ShellExpr) (List ShellStage) (List ShellCmd)
    | ScSetIndex (Text) (ShellExpr) (ShellExpr)
    | ScSetWritable (ShellExpr)
    | ScCallMethod (ShellExpr) (Text) (List ShellExpr)
    | ScEchoStyled (ShellExpr) (ShellColor) (Boolean)
    | ScThrow (ShellExpr)
    | ScWaitProcessFor (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScStopProcess (ShellExpr)
    | ScSleepMs (ShellExpr)
    | ScWaitProcessSec (Text) (ShellExpr)
    | ScDeleteTree (ShellExpr)
    | ScEchoPartial (ShellExpr)
    | ScRaw (Text)

Section: Process Spec

  ShellProcessSpec = record {
    sp-executable : ShellExpr,
    sp-arguments : List ShellExpr,
    sp-result-var : Text,
    sp-stdout-file : Maybe ShellExpr,
    sp-stderr-file : Maybe ShellExpr,
    sp-hidden : Boolean,
    sp-passthru : Boolean
  }

Section: Parameters

  ShellParamType =
    | SptString
    | SptInt
    | SptSwitch
    | SptBool
    | SptPath
    | SptStringArray
    | SptLong

 sp-choices constrains a parameter to a fixed set. An empty list means
 unconstrained. A shell that refuses a value the script cannot handle
 refuses it at the boundary, before anything downstream has looked for a
 file named after it.

  ShellParam = record {
    sp-name : Text,
    sp-type : ShellParamType,
    sp-mandatory : Boolean,
    sp-default : Maybe ShellExpr,
    sp-choices : List Text
  }

Section: Script

  ShellScript = record {
    ss-name : Text,
    ss-description : Text,
    ss-params : List ShellParam,
    ss-body : List ShellCmd
  }

